### Sample webhook requests (VS Code "REST Client" / JetBrains HTTP client).
### Start the app first:  npm run db:seed && npm run dev
### These run UNSIGNED, which the server accepts only when no secrets are configured (dev mode).
### With secrets set, use scripts/send-fixtures.sh instead: it signs each body with HMAC-SHA256.
### Sending the same receipt twice by different routes (WhatsApp, then email) is not an error: the second one goes to review as a possible duplicate.
### The "files" are fixtures/documents/<name>.fixture (bytes: the ASCII string "DARB-FIXTURE:<name>"); the mock extractor looks them up by SHA-256.
### WhatsApp media ids (media_4471, ...) are resolved through fixtures/media-map.json. Print every fixture's hash/base64:  npx tsx scripts/print-fixtures.ts

@base = http://localhost:3000

### 1. Email, exact match from Desert Fleet's mailbox   -> AUTO_MATCHED to txn_email
POST {{base}}/api/webhooks/email
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "messageId": "<http-1@desertfleet>",
  "from": "accounts@desertfleet.example",
  "to": ["receipts@darb.sa"],
  "subject": "Tax invoice INV-88231",
  "attachments": [
    { "filename": "invoice.jpg", "contentType": "image/jpeg", "contentBase64": "REFSQi1GSVhUVVJFOmVtYWlsX2V4YWN0" }
  ]
}

### 2. Same message again (redelivery)   -> 200, "duplicate": true, nothing new stored
POST {{base}}/api/webhooks/email
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "messageId": "<http-1@desertfleet>",
  "from": "accounts@desertfleet.example",
  "to": ["receipts@darb.sa"],
  "attachments": [
    { "filename": "invoice.jpg", "contentType": "image/jpeg", "contentBase64": "REFSQi1GSVhUVVJFOmVtYWlsX2V4YWN0" }
  ]
}

### 3. Email from an unregistered sender   -> 200 {"status":"ignored","reason":"UNKNOWN_SENDER"}, nothing stored
POST {{base}}/api/webhooks/email
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "messageId": "<http-3@evil>",
  "from": "stranger@evil.example",
  "to": ["receipts@darb.sa"],
  "attachments": [
    { "filename": "x.jpg", "contentType": "image/jpeg", "contentBase64": "REFSQi1GSVhUVVJFOmV4YWN0" }
  ]
}

### 4. Invalid payload   -> 400 with field paths only (never echoes submitted values)
POST {{base}}/api/webhooks/email
Content-Type: application/json

{ "messageId": "", "from": "not-an-email", "to": [], "attachments": [] }

### 5. WhatsApp handshake (Meta calls this when you subscribe the webhook). Needs WHATSAPP_VERIFY_TOKEN set.
GET {{base}}/api/webhooks/whatsapp?hub.mode=subscribe&hub.verify_token=YOUR_TOKEN&hub.challenge=1158201444

### 6. WhatsApp image from driver +966 50 111 1111   -> AUTO_MATCHED to txn_exact
###    The media id media_4471 (fixtures/documents/exact.fixture) is resolved by a dev-only fixture MediaStore (no Meta credentials needed).
POST {{base}}/api/webhooks/whatsapp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "object": "whatsapp_business_account",
  "entry": [{
    "id": "WABA_ID",
    "changes": [{
      "field": "messages",
      "value": {
        "messaging_product": "whatsapp",
        "metadata": { "display_phone_number": "15550001111", "phone_number_id": "123" },
        "messages": [{
          "id": "wamid.http-1",
          "from": "966501111111",
          "timestamp": "1760000000",
          "type": "image",
          "image": { "id": "media_4471", "mime_type": "image/jpeg" }
        }]
      }
    }]
  }]
}

### 7. WhatsApp: two same-amount, same-day, same-merchant transactions   -> NEEDS_REVIEW (open http://localhost:3000/review)
POST {{base}}/api/webhooks/whatsapp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "object": "whatsapp_business_account",
  "entry": [{ "id": "W", "changes": [{ "field": "messages", "value": {
    "messaging_product": "whatsapp", "metadata": { "phone_number_id": "123" },
    "messages": [{ "id": "wamid.http-2", "from": "966501111111", "timestamp": "1760000000", "type": "image",
                   "image": { "id": "media_4472", "mime_type": "image/jpeg" } }]
  } }] }]
}

### 8. WhatsApp delivery receipts only (no messages)   -> 200 {"status":"ignored","reason":"NO_MEDIA"}
POST {{base}}/api/webhooks/whatsapp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "object": "whatsapp_business_account",
  "entry": [{ "id": "W", "changes": [{ "field": "messages", "value": {
    "messaging_product": "whatsapp", "metadata": { "phone_number_id": "123" },
    "statuses": [{ "id": "wamid.x", "status": "delivered" }]
  } }] }]
}

### 9. Card transaction feed: delivers a transaction; UNMATCHED receipts in the same scope are re-matched
POST {{base}}/api/webhooks/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

[{
  "externalRef": "feed-http-1",
  "clientId": "client_alnoor",
  "driverPhone": "+966501111111",
  "merchantName": "SAUDI ELECTRICITY CO",
  "amountMinor": 99999,
  "currency": "SAR",
  "occurredAt": "2026-10-02T10:00:00+03:00"
}]


### The assignment's own sample payloads. The bodies are fixtures/webhooks/*.json (real bytes instead of the <base64> placeholder).

### 10. Assignment email sample: `to` is a plain string, from billing@alfanar-fuel.com.sa (a demo mailbox of Al Noor in the seed)
###     -> 200 accepted; the tax invoice is OCR'd and AUTO_MATCHED to txn_alfanar ("ALFANAR FUEL ST 04 RUH" = "Alfanar Fuel Station", 287.50)
POST {{base}}/api/webhooks/email
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "messageId": "msg_8f2a1",
  "from": "billing@alfanar-fuel.com.sa",
  "to": "receipts@darb.example.com",
  "subject": "Tax Invoice #INV-99812",
  "receivedAt": "2025-06-14T09:21:00Z",
  "attachments": [
    {
      "filename": "invoice-99812.pdf",
      "contentType": "application/pdf",
      "contentBase64": "REFSQi1GSVhUVVJFOmFsZmFuYXJfaW52b2ljZQ=="
    }
  ]
}

### 11. The same sample with the literal "<base64>" placeholder   -> 400 naming attachments.0.contentBase64 (never a 500)
POST {{base}}/api/webhooks/email
Content-Type: application/json

{"messageId":"msg_8f2a1","from":"billing@alfanar-fuel.com.sa","to":"receipts@darb.example.com","subject":"Tax Invoice #INV-99812","receivedAt":"2025-06-14T09:21:00Z","attachments":[{"filename":"invoice-99812.pdf","contentType":"application/pdf","contentBase64":"<base64>"}]}

### 12. Assignment WhatsApp sample: no object / entry.id / field / messaging_product / metadata, from 966551234567
###     -> 200 accepted; that number is not a seeded driver, so the document is stored and ends UNMATCHED (NO_CANDIDATES_IN_SCOPE)
POST {{base}}/api/webhooks/whatsapp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "entry": [
    {
      "changes": [
        {
          "value": {
            "messages": [
              {
                "id": "wamid.HBgMOTY2NT...",
                "from": "966551234567",
                "timestamp": "1718356881",
                "type": "image",
                "image": {
                  "id": "media_4471",
                  "mime_type": "image/jpeg",
                  "sha256": "a3f1c9..."
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

### 13. A restaurant receipt of 57.50 against a card charge of 63.25 (tip), from driver +966 50 222 2222
###     -> NEEDS_REVIEW (TIP_SUSPECTED) for txn_restaurant; open http://localhost:3000/review
POST {{base}}/api/webhooks/whatsapp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "entry": [
    {
      "changes": [
        {
          "value": {
            "messages": [
              {
                "id": "wamid.HBgMOTY2NT.tip",
                "from": "966502222222",
                "timestamp": "1718356881",
                "type": "image",
                "image": { "id": "media_4485", "mime_type": "image/jpeg" }
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
